        "id": 16278,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-06T01:13:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So I'm playing against Voss with the Sentinels and Mr. Fixer on the team. Fixer has Dual Crowbars, GMF and Harmony out, so Writhe hits him with Black Out -- except he only got one follow-up shot, instead of having a second attack after each of the 2+ attacks. So what gives? Isn't he supposed to do one after each? Is this a bug?</p><p>EDIT: Okay, same game, and Sky-Scraper played Catch a Ride on Mr. Fixer -- the first blow from the Crowbars killed a minion, while the second hit the transporter, which survived, but Sky-Scraper's blow never came. I thought previous rulings said that you could pick one of the two to hit, but this didn't even give the option?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:56.724Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
