      {
        "id": 191464,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-11T23:52:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don’t see a problem with that</p>\n<p>I also don’t see how that’s true. You’re still dealing damage. It’s a second instance of damage, caused by the same initial effect, but it’s still a new instance of damage. There are no simultaneous​ actions in game, so I don’t see why “Sky-Scraper deals one Target dealt damage this way” doesn’t apply to Crowbars.</p>",
        "post_number": 9,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:18:02.821Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
