      {
        "id": 191465,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-12T00:32:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It's a difference in how Dual Crowbars and Jack Handle work. &nbsp;Catch a Ride with Jack Handle lets you pick any target since Jack Handle took the original damage and applied it to all non-hero targets. &nbsp; Dual Crowbars is only using that first instance of damage with the intial hit and that hit causes Dual Crowbars to allow Fixer to hit another target. &nbsp; Since the second hit was a reaction to the first hit the second part of Catch a Ride will only do damage if the intial target is still standing. &nbsp; Again I'll go back to the case with Friendly Fire. &nbsp; The targets you hit with Jack Handle doesn't allow you to trigger Friendly Fire again but with Dual Crowbars the first attack on Setback causes a second reactionary hit which allows you to trigger Friendly Fire again as it is seen as a new hit not associated with original hit on Setback. &nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 10,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:18:02.882Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
