        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>It&#39;s a difference in how Dual Crowbars and Jack Handle work. &nbsp;Catch a Ride with Jack Handle lets you pick any target since Jack Handle took the original damage and applied it to all non-hero targets. &nbsp; Dual Crowbars is only using that first instance of damage with the intial hit and that hit causes Dual Crowbars to allow Fixer to hit another target. &nbsp; Since the second hit was a reaction to the first hit the second part of Catch a Ride will only do damage if the intial target is still standing. &nbsp; Again I&#39;ll go back to the case with Friendly Fire. &nbsp; The targets you hit with Jack Handle doesn&#39;t allow you to trigger Friendly Fire again but with Dual Crowbars the first attack on Setback causes a second reactionary hit which allows you to trigger Friendly Fire again as it is seen as a new hit not associated with original hit on Setback. &nbsp;</p>",
